{"/api/discogs/artist/10407/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"10407","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Kohf2pN6fahGk2hY72zc1_RPk1Oqglz96xIdN5x2SpU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:449/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNDA3/LTE0ODAxMDgxMTAt/NjY1MS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Hzeon7xIGnnRlzQ22XHwSB3a8r64qhF1_nIRwZNkfHw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNDA3/LTE0ODAxMDgxMTAt/NjY1MS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Paul Harris, Steve Smith and Ben Harris are three lads from Kent and the South London suburbs with very different musical backgrounds, united by a shared love of a good tune and a passion for partying.\r\n\r\nPaul Harris started clubbing in his early teens and bagged his first professional DJ gig when he was 17, just before acid house took dance culture mainstream. He gradually began spending more time mixing and making records than playing them, but has continued to be successful as a DJ.\r\n\r\nA drummer since schooldays, Steve Smith gave up his job in the print trade during the rave explosion when he realized he could make more money playing live percussion in clubs at weekends. By the mid-90s he was playing in a band called Higher Ground, and when the singer left he reluctantly stepped in, discovering with some surprise that he had a fine voice. When the band fell apart he went to Ibiza to write, but then a chance meeting with Paul at an airport on the way to a club event led to a wild weekend, and the idea of making music together.\r\n\r\nBen Harris (no relation to Paul) played guitar in indie rock band Fluid until they did their first demo and he saw how the engineer worked the mixing desk. He got a job in a recording studio, \"got bitten by the dance bug\", and ended up running a specialist dance record shop in Bromley with his brother. After producing a string of successful one-off club tunes he began working with Paul, who a few weeks later bumped into Steve and invited him to join them.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:10407","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":99793,"name":"Paul Harris"},{"active":true,"id":136536,"name":"Steve Smith (2)"},{"active":false,"id":152168,"name":"Ben Harris"}],"namevariations":["Dirty Harry","Dirty Vegas (Ben Harris, Steve Smith, Paul Harris)","Dirty Vegas (Paul Harris/Steve Smith/Ben Harris)","DirtyVegas","Ditry Vegas","賭城老千"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/10407-Dirty-Vegas","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.dirtyvegas.com","http://dirtyvegasmusic.bandcamp.com","http://www.bandsintown.com/DirtyVegas","http://www.facebook.com/dirtyvegasmusic","http://instagram.com/dirtyvegasmusic","http://www.myspace.com/dirtyvegas","http://soundcloud.com/dirtyvegas","http://www.youtube.com/user/DirtyVegasVEVO","http://www.youtube.com/user/OfficialDirtyVegas"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1536956/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1536956","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Jn6lid3gupT7Olaag6MYM0sqBLA9kOcvyIO9q6WewCk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:438/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1MzY5/NTYtMTY2MjY1OTky/Ny05ODQzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/MoHAIrL4_71qWUhwv4nO2zb5RNSn9QDlwKBbPmra6JI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1MzY5/NTYtMTY2MjY1OTky/Ny05ODQzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1536956","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":46674,"name":"Aaron Jerome"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["SBTRKT","Sbstrk"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1536956-Sbtrkt","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.sbtrkt.com/","https://www.saveyourself.tv","http://www.facebook.com/SBTRKT","http://twitter.com/SBTRKT","http://myspace.com/subtractone","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SBTRKT","http://www.whosampled.com/SBTRKT/","http://soundcloud.com/sbtrkt","http://www.youtube.com/user/SBTRKT","http://www.youtube.com/user/SBTRKTVEVO","http://equipboard.com/pros/sbtrkt","https://sbtrkt.bandcamp.com"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/207341/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"207341","image":"https://i.discogs.com/UbwEKpbPvXCjsw8viXBWkeKOM3sxXa-8G4bf1JeG8no/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIwNzM0/MS0xMzIyNjY2MTIy/LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/U33eZ034w7wvGRNHSoSokif9qdU8UssQoV37CUAh9qo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIwNzM0/MS0xMzIyNjY2MTIy/LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"DJ and producer from Germany. Co-founder of the Berlin-based label [l=Best Works Records].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:207341","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Andre Lodeman","Andre Lodemann","Andre' Lodemann","Andre` Lodemann","Lodemann"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/207341-André-Lodemann","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/andrelodemann","http://www.facebook.com/pages/Andre-Lodemann/116280615064308","http://www.soundcloud.com/lodemann"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2866978/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2866978","image":"https://i.discogs.com/h60smP5Mj52de1vo7WtqVkYkYzSWDQfJKkQgu2cv7Uc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:382/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI4NjY5/NzgtMTcwODUzMTE1/NC0xMDI0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/F6x-IafrBS4FYSomQvrOSIbodXpQEhRPkNYggqeGgro/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI4NjY5/NzgtMTcwODUzMTE1/NC0xMDI0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Sarah Farina sprinkles positivity over the darkest bass. She’s innovative, she’s skilful, and she’s the smiling antithesis of genre cliques and sour scene elitists. What you hear is all you need to know. And what you’ll hear from Sarah Farina’s sets and music productions are seamlessly blended bass-heavy frequencies and futuristic beats with fearless forays through the hardcore continuum and beyond.\r\n\r\nIt’s inclusive, forward-thinking and unrestrained. It’s a genre-rejecting style that she’s named RainbowBass.\r\n\r\nLed by the early releases of Missy Elliott, Aphex Twin & J Dilla into the clubs of Berlin. She hosts her own interdisciplinary Berlin event series „Emergent Bass“ with her friends, which focuses on the historical awareness of cultural contexts of music and celebrates and uplifts the Afro-diasporic influences in the underground club culture.\r\n\r\nShe’s vocal about the issues of current club culture and runs the project Transmission with Dr. Kerstin Meißner, which aims to make the political relevance and history of international sound, club and rave culture audible and visible.\r\n\r\nShe has been teaching and hosting DJ workshops in Rwanda, Uganda, Alexandria, Detroit & many other places, always with the focus on cultivating joy within her workshops and showing that music, DJing and club culture can be so much more than just producing or consuming it.\r\n\r\nSarah Farina is recognised and revered by the best of her bass music contemporaries, with connections to crews worldwide including Underground Resistance, Teklife, Hyperdub, Deep Medi, Buraka Som Sistema, Modeselektor and Exit Records. Capable of holding her own in line-ups alongside artists as diverse as DJ Rashad (RIP), DJ Storm, Laurent Garnier, Kode9, François K and Lady Leshurr, her sets unite the dance floor, equally impressive to industry insiders and those who just want to dance.\r\n\r\nA listen to any of her three acclaimed Boiler Room sets will demonstrate why she’s captured the rapt attention of tastemakers and influencers the whole world over. A music producer and DJ with tighter-than-a-drum mixes and flawless selections is hard to find. You just found one.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2866978","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2866978-Sarah-Farina","type":"artist","urls":["http://sarahfarina.com/","https://www.instagram.com/sarahfarinabln","https://sarahfarina.bandcamp.com/","https://soundcloud.com/sarahfarina","https://ra.co/dj/sarahfarina","https://www.facebook.com/sarahfarinabln","https://twitter.com/sarahfarinabln"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/29922/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"29922","image":"https://i.discogs.com/bC53E6ujJDknHEI9ok1wGTlpwWTRlffj-WV5G6JXg3Q/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5OTIy/LTE2OTA0NzA5NzMt/MTQxNC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/W9BPmqo3Muiw_GeEsxa-bOZKfqDW3AgrirszWa5lgvY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5OTIy/LTE2OTA0NzA5NzMt/MTQxNC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Former, American model Betty Davis (born July 26, 1944 in Durham, North Carolina; died February 9, 2022 in Homestead, Pennsylvania) was an American funk and soul singer. She was known for her memorable live performances. \r\n\r\nShe was married to [a=Miles Davis] from September 1968 until 1970.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:29922","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1076460,"name":"Betty Mabry"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["B. Davis","B.Davis","Bette Davis","Davis"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/29922-Betty-Davis","type":"artist","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betty_Davis","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm10140175/","https://www.facebook.com/pages/Betty-Davis/110193019060912","https://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=114171958","https://bettydavis.bandcamp.com","https://www.whosampled.com/Betty-Davis/","https://www.milesdavis.com/albums/filles-de-kilimanjaro/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/41513/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"41513","image":"https://i.discogs.com/T7BorE6Sy0SQElwlWseQz8y_gybSQNrnq9Ny4EvLTZw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:184/w:252/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQxNTEz/LTExMjc5MjM3MzIu/anBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/VBSQzmMShYz_h6ylcFgs4qPT6yRGq1G9LHaJZ0d3KQw/rs:fi